{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1414393-books-from-other-game-lines-with-changeling-content","id":1414393,"title":"Books from other game lines with Changeling content?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-18T07:28:24-07:00","id":1414393,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Books from other game lines with Changeling content?","content":"I've been trying to put together a list of books for other WoD games that still have relevant Changeling content, but it's kind of hard to find definitive information about which books have what. Here's what I have, and I was hoping others would be able to add to it, or offer opinions on what should be here?<br /> <br /> I'm kind of trying to find examples of places that have Actual New Information you might want if you're reading with a C:tD focus. So like, not every single setting book which lists a random changeling in the collection of NPCs at the end, or storyteller conversion guides for including changelings in <i>other</i> games. Unless, of course, that stuff is, for some reason, unique or interesting!<br /> <br /> <b>Stuff I Think For Sure Counts As Having Changeling Stuff:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Blood-dimmed Tides:</b> rules for the merfolk kith.<br /> <b>WoD: Combat:</b> small selection of Changeling-specific combat rules (around using cantrips while fighting), Changeling is a named game line for which the book can be used, and they are occasionally referenced in the game text (i.e. that kithain nobles favour fencing, etc.<br /> <b>Midnight Circus:</b> adventure designed to be usable with any of the first five game lines. <br /> <b>Bygone Bestiary: </b>includes chimerical critters.<br /> <b>Time of Judgment: </b>game line wrap up for Changeling.<br /> <b>Werewolf: Rage Across Appalachia: </b>new Nunnehi kith. <br /> <br /> <b>Does It Count...?:</b><br /> <br /> <b>WoD: Gypsies:</b> no rules for Changeling, though Gypsy characters may have fae blood and rules are included for this. Also, just to put it out there, this book feels super sketchy to me in terms of cultural appropriation. (Not that it'd be the first time for a WoD property but, I just felt I should say it. Not super duper sure I want it in my collection.)<br /> <b>WoD: Hong Kong:</b> primarily a V:tM sourcebook, but notes that information for other major games is included. Practically this seems to be limited to the odd description here and there and a collection of NPCs...?<br /> <b>WoD: Tokyo:</b> as above, except primarily a W:tO sourcebook. Again, advertises that crossover information is available for other games, but this seems limited and mostly stats for NPCs...?<br /> <b>KotE: Blood &amp; Silk: </b>a Dark Ages sourcebook for Kindred of the East, but it does include setting and crossover information for other gamelines in that era/area, including the Hsien. I'm torn, on the one hand, this feels similar to the sections at the back of a lot of core rulebooks which outline the other supernaturals and the subject-of-the-book's attitudes towards them with some loose rules for including them. On the other, it's actual historical setting information <i>not</i> available elsewhere from the POV of the Hsien themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>What am I missing?</b><br /> <br /> Any ideas? I know the Fianna and Kiasyd have tied to the fae - is this detailed in any splatbooks? Is it cool? Is it worth looking at? Halp! I must read ALLLL the books!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T09:22:38-07:00","id":1414411,"title":"","content":"WoD: Gypsies predated Changeling and so has no Changeling content.<br /> <br /> The big three are Blood Dimmed Tides, The Bygone Bestiary, and RA Appalachia (it was the introduction of the Duchy of Appalachia and the Cherokee spirit people), along with Time of Judgment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 09-18-2020, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T23:19:20-07:00","id":1414511,"title":"","content":"Ah - interesting, thank you. I hadn't noticed the publication date, but you're right of course. Gypsies was 94, and C:tD came out in 95. Though I do think the author was likely aware of the plan for it since there's a specific background/power tied to faerie blood? At least I'm about 80% sure. I've looked through a friend's copy, but obviously at the moment the good old days of Going Over To A Friend's House are gone... Either way it's a tidy line. <br /> <br /> Also glad to know I'm not missing anything major in terms of the other books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[]